    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the only thing stopping us from total chaos is the threat of state violence, doesn't that mean the \"order\" we have is actually just built on fear rather than actual morality? i'm trying to see if there's a way to argue that a society based on coercion is inherently less \"civilized\" than one based on purely voluntary exchange, even if the voluntary one is more \"chaotic.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
